# Documentation

Permanent truth is `documentation/` plus `memory.md`. Do not cite `ai-input/` as the live source of truth.

## After a completed change, update

- The matching `documentation/features/*.md`
- `documentation/api/*` if endpoints changed
- `documentation/database/*` if schema changed
- `documentation/architecture/*` or `documentation/security/*` if those changed
- An ADR under `documentation/decisions/` for material architecture, security, database, auth, or dependency decisions
- `memory.md` for phase, stack, feature status, API/DB/security/UI decisions, bugs, debt, pending work

## Rules

- Keep Confirmed / Proposed / Open Question labels honest.
- Do not invent fields or endpoints in docs to match speculative code.
- Do not fabricate ADR “Approved By”.
- `docs/` at repo root is empty legacy; do not treat it as the OS.
- Record Change History on feature files when behavior changes.
